- A **regulator gene (i gene)** that codes for the **repressor** protein;
- The **operator** (o), a DNA segment where the repressor binds;
- The **promoter** (p), which binds RNA polymerase;
- Three **structural genes**: **z**, which codes for $\beta$-galactosidase (breaks lactose into glucose and galactose), **y**, which codes for **permease** (increases permeability of the cell to lactose), and **a**, which codes for **transacetylase**.
